==============================================================================
STEP 0: transverse unit vectors are EXACT (|alpha(1-w_t)|^2 = 1 for N(alpha)=t)
==============================================================================
  t=2: no Eisenstein alpha with N=2 (not Loeschian) -> no transverse vectors
  t=3: alpha=(-2, 1) (N=3), |alpha(1-w_t)|^2 = (Fraction(1, 1), Fraction(0, 1), Fraction(0, 1), Fraction(0, 1))  -> unit: True
  t=4: alpha=(-2, 0) (N=4), |alpha(1-w_t)|^2 = (Fraction(1, 1), Fraction(0, 1), Fraction(0, 1), Fraction(0, 1))  -> unit: True
  t=13: alpha=(-4, 1) (N=13), |alpha(1-w_t)|^2 = (Fraction(1, 1), Fraction(0, 1), Fraction(0, 1), Fraction(0, 1))  -> unit: True

==============================================================================
STEP 1: resonance bonus on small patches (Moser angle t=3, the Moser lattice)
==============================================================================
--- rhombus [] rhombus  (t=3, D=11, w_t=Moser angle, |G|=4 e(G)=5, |H|=4 e(H)=5) ---
  product points: 16 (coincident: 0)
  generic-angle (Cartesian product) unit distances : e(G)|H|+|G|e(H) = 40
  Moser-angle exact unit distances (brute, exact)  : 41
  resonance bonus  Delta = actual - generic        : 1
  formula  sum_{N(a)=t} m_a(G)m_a(H) / 2          : 1
  MATCH: True
  avgdeg generic = 5.0000 ; avgdeg Moser = 5.1250  (kappa=6)

--- rosette W7 [] rhombus  (t=3, D=11, w_t=Moser angle, |G|=7 e(G)=12, |H|=4 e(H)=5) ---
  product points: 28 (coincident: 0)
  generic-angle (Cartesian product) unit distances : e(G)|H|+|G|e(H) = 83
  Moser-angle exact unit distances (brute, exact)  : 85
  resonance bonus  Delta = actual - generic        : 2
  formula  sum_{N(a)=t} m_a(G)m_a(H) / 2          : 2
  MATCH: True
  avgdeg generic = 5.9286 ; avgdeg Moser = 6.0714  (kappa=6)

--- rosette W7 [] rosette W7  (t=3, D=11, w_t=Moser angle, |G|=7 e(G)=12, |H|=7 e(H)=12) ---
  product points: 49 (coincident: 0)
